Thought: To simulate the melting of copper, I need to follow a series of steps: retrieve the structure of copper, convert it to a LAMMPS data file, select the appropriate potential, create a LAMMPS input script, run the simulation, and finally extract the final density. First, I'll retrieve the structure of copper using the given Materials Project ID.
Action: get_structure_from_mp_text
Action Input: {"mp_id": "mp-30", "file_path": "/results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/react/melting/comprehensive/tasks/copper_melting_trial_4/copper_structure.cif"}

Thought: The structure of copper has been successfully retrieved and saved as a CIF file. Next, I will convert this CIF file into a LAMMPS data file, which is necessary for running the simulation.
Action: convert_structure_to_lammps_data
Action Input: {"structure_path": "/results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/react/melting/comprehensive/tasks/copper_melting_trial_4/copper_structure.cif", "output_file": "/results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/react/melting/comprehensive/tasks/copper_melting_trial_4/copper_structure.data", "atom_style": "atomic"}

